f->used << factor;
```
Reason:
The original logic incorrectly used left shifts to calculate `units_32`, `avail_32`, and `used_32`, which caused the values to exceed the 32-bit integer limit when handling large filesystems (greater than 8 TB). This resulted in incorrect values being assigned to these variables.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
f->units_32 = f->units << shift;
f->avail_32 = f->avail >> shift;
f->used_32 = f->used >> shift;
```
Reason:
The patch corrects the handling of large filesystem sizes by using right shifts for `avail_32` and `used_32`, and left shifts for `units_32`, based on the number of shifts needed to bring the size within the 32-bit range. This ensures that the values remain valid and do not exceed the limits of 32-bit integers.

